{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Surely HaShem is in this place, etc.</b> He mentioned the word מָקוֹם three times, corresponding to the three Temples. Corresponding to the First Temple, where the Shekhinah dwelt and yet even so they did not know HaShem, for after their idols their heart went — concerning this he said, 'Surely HaShem is in this place and I did not know it.' Corresponding to the Second Temple it says, 'How awesome is this place; this is none other than the house of Elohim,' for it is known that in the Second Temple there was the awe of the Sanctuary upon all the nations, for even Alexander Macedon was afraid to lay a hand on it, and he would rise to his feet because of Shimon the Righteous, even though five essential things were lacking in it: the Shekhinah, and prophecy, and the Ark, and the Urim and Thummim, and the heavenly fire, and there remained in it only the Name, for it was called the house of Elohim. Concerning this he said here, 'this is none other than the house of Elohim,' for in the First Temple HaShem appeared to them eye to eye, so that they would point to His glory, blessed be He, saying, ״זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ״ (Exodus 15:2), ״הִנֵּה אֱלֹהֵינוּ זֶה״ (Isaiah 25:9). But in the Second Temple, 'this is not' — and there remained in it only the Name, which is 'the house of Elohim.' Corresponding to the Third Temple he said, 'And he called the name of that place Beth-El; but Luz was the name of the city at first,' as though the name Luz was never uprooted from it after it was destroyed following its building. But in the future its building will be eternal, for the calling of the name indicates eternal permanence, ״וְזֶה שְּׁמוֹ לְעוֹלָם״ (Exodus 3:15), and as it says ״וְשֵׁם הָעִיר מִיּוֹם ה׳ שָׁמָּה״ (Ezekiel 48:35). The Radak explained that this means that forever His name, blessed be He, will never depart from within it." "And likewise at the beginning of the parashah, three times the word מָקוֹם: corresponding to the First Temple, he said, 'And he encountered the place and lodged there because the sun had come' — for the days did not lengthen for them there but only the measure of a single night's lodging; this, their dwelling in the Temple was brief, an allusion to the shortness of the time the Temple stood in its holiness, 'until the sun came,' for ״שֶׁמֶשׁ וְיָרֵחַ אָסְפוּ נָגְהָם״ (Joel 2:10), and above we have explained the matter of its setting two hours before its proper time, an allusion to the setting of the sun of Israel two years before the appointed time. Corresponding to the Second Temple, he said, 'And he took from the stones of the place,' for so it is said of the building of the Second Temple, ״וְהוֹצִיא אֶת הָאֶבֶן הָרֹאשָׁה״ etc. (Zechariah 4:7), and 'from the stones' and not 'all the stones,' for the stones of the Tablets and the stones of the Urim and Thummim were lacking. Corresponding to the Third Temple, he said, 'And he lay down in that place,' for when he saw the Third Temple in its building and its eternity, then he lay down and his sleep was sweet, as if to say, ״זֹאת מְנוּחָתִי עֲדֵי עַד״, to exclude the first two Temples, in which they did not rest from their enemies."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:57.010427614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}